# Press catalog corrections

When fixing Omeka titles, descriptions, or bag metadata for a press-material item:

## Ledger `game_key` is the full package id

Do **not** guess a short slug (`avengers-initiative`). Ledger **`game_key`** is **`package_id`**: `{title-slug}-{uuid}` (see `docs/config-contract.md`).

**Always resolve from Postgres first** (`hitsave_ledger`, table `game_ingest`):

```sql
SELECT game_key, omeka_item_id, moby_title, aip_wasabi_prefix
FROM game_ingest
WHERE omeka_item_id = <item_id>;
-- or: WHERE game_key LIKE 'avengers-initiative-%'
```

## Patch script (Omeka + Wasabi bag)

**Status-web (preferred):** `http://<host>:8090/correct?omeka_ref=<id>` — form triggers Windmill **`f/hitsave/correct_catalog_item`** (same bash wrapper as the Windmill UI; requires `ops.windmill` + token in `status-web.yaml`). **`execute`** defaults to **true** for Wasabi bag sync when title or Moby URL changes.

**Windmill (optional):** `f/hitsave/correct_catalog_item` — same fields for scheduled/automation use.

**Manual quarantine:** status-web **`/quarantine`** or Windmill **`f/hitsave/quarantine_catalog_item`** — wraps `curation-quarantine-omeka.py` (`--omeka-ref`, `--reason`, note).

**CLI:** `scripts/correct-catalog-item.py` (same flags as `--omeka-ref`, `--title`, …). Wrong Moby match: `--clear-moby-url` (resets description to press-kit text unless `--description` is set; clears creator/publisher unless `--developer` / `--publisher` is set; ledger Moby reset defaults on). Status-web leaves description blank when clearing Moby so the CLI can restore press-kit text (do not pass an empty `--description`).

Press-specific one-shot (all fields required) remains **`patch-press-catalog-omeka-and-bag.py`**. Prefer **`--omeka-item-id`** (from ARK name segment or public API) so the script loads the correct **`game_key`**:

```bash
docker compose run --rm --entrypoint python omeka-catalog \
  /app/scripts/patch-press-catalog-omeka-and-bag.py \
  --omeka-item-id 27710 \
  --title 'Marvel: Avengers Initiative' \
  --former-title 'Avengers Initiative' \
  --reference-uri 'https://www.mobygames.com/game/76444' \
  --description 'Press material for Marvel: Avengers Initiative.' \
  --correction-summary '…' \
  --execute
```

Dry-run: omit **`--execute`**. Use **`--game-key`** only when you already copied the full key from the ledger.

## Post-ingest quarantine (wallpaper / policy)

Hide a live catalog row and set ledger **`status=quarantine`**:

```bash
docker compose run --rm --entrypoint python omeka-catalog \
  /app/scripts/curation-quarantine-omeka.py \
  --omeka-item-id 27706 \
  --reason hash_named_images \
  Single md5-named JPEG; not press-kit material (Avatar TLA wallpaper).
```

Use **`block_reason`** codes aligned with ingest **`content_policy`** (`hash_named_images`, `booru_tagged_filenames`, …).

## After Omeka-only API edits

If you patched Omeka without the script, still run the script with **`--omeka-item-id`** and **`--execute`** so **`metadata/submission.json`**, **`bag-info.txt`**, and **`tagmanifest-sha256.txt`** on Wasabi stay aligned (re-register will not revert titles if generated batch YAML on the preservation host is updated separately).
